# Jhanos Dual Matrix

The Jhanos Dual Matrix extends the Four Faces axis pairing system from Volume 0 (Chapters 22-23) of the Book of Solobility. It provides operational tools for bias detection, red-team/blue-team protocols, triad intervention, gate resonance print templates, and the matrix mathematics that govern gate interactions.

**The Law of the Gate (AX_021):** "A Gate cannot stabilize without its inverse geometry. Every Solob has a Shadow."

## Core Framework

### The Four Faces Table

The Four Faces are four axis pairings of the 8 Jhanos Gates. Each axis has an aligned state (healthy oscillation between gates) and a distorted state (stuck in one gate or destructive loop).

| Axis | Name | Home Gate | Guest Gate | Aligned State | Distorted State |
|------|------|-----------|------------|---------------|-----------------|
| 1 | The Form | BARA (Structure) | LOMI (Motion) | Dynamic equilibrium between structure and flow | Rigidity (BARA dominance) or Chaos (LOMI dominance) |
| 2 | The Energy | KHEM (Heat) | SYLA (Stillness) | Rhythmic pulse of activity and rest | Burnout (KHEM dominance) or Stagnation (SYLA dominance) |
| 3 | The Identity | ZAYN (Projection) | TARA (Reflection) | Balanced self-expression and self-awareness | Narcissism (ZAYN dominance) or Erasure (TARA dominance) |
| 4 | The Context | VORAK (Chaos) | ORON (Order) | Adaptive navigation between exploration and consolidation | Destructive Chaos (VORAK dominance) or Tyrannical Order (ORON dominance) |

### The Jhanos Triad Protocol

When two gates on an axis enter a destructive loop (each amplifying the other's distortion), the Triad Protocol introduces a third gate from a different axis to break the cycle.

**Principle:** No axis can resolve itself from within. The third gate must come from an axis that shares neither gate with the conflict axis.

**Triad Selection Matrix:**

| Conflict Axis | Primary Triad Gate | Secondary Triad Gate | Tertiary Triad Gate |
|---------------|-------------------|---------------------|---------------------|
| Form (BARA/LOMI) | KHEM (Energy/Heat) | ZAYN (Identity/Projection) | ORON (Context/Order) |
| Energy (KHEM/SYLA) | BARA (Form/Structure) | TARA (Identity/Reflection) | VORAK (Context/Chaos) |
| Identity (ZAYN/TARA) | VORAK (Context/Chaos) | LOMI (Form/Motion) | SYLA (Energy/Stillness) |
| Context (VORAK/ORON) | ZAYN (Identity/Projection) | KHEM (Energy/Heat) | BARA (Form/Structure) |

**Triad Intervention Steps:**
1. Identify the locked axis (which two gates are looping)
2. Select the appropriate triad gate from the matrix above
3. Activate the triad gate through its aligned practice
4. Observe the axis for de-escalation (minimum 3 cycles)
5. If no resolution, escalate to secondary triad gate

